 the checkpoint\n34\t    session_id?: string, exact host-provided session identifier (pair with agent)\n35\t    agent?: string, agent harness identifier such as tau or claude-code or codex\n36\t    tau_session_id?: string, legacy Tau session identifier (read compatibility only)\n37\t    claude_session_id?: string, legacy Claude Code session identifier (read compatibility only)\n38\t    codex_session_id?: string, legacy Codex session identifier (read compatibility only)\n39\t    codex_turn_id?: string, Codex turn identifier\n40\t    trigger?: string, compaction trigger or deliberate checkpoint source\n41\t    model?: string, active model slug when known\n42\t    capture?(enum, how this checkpoint was produced): [extractive, deliberate, summarized]\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t# Coding Session\n46\t\n47\tA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\n48\tidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\n49\tfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n50\t\n51\tExamples:\n52\t\n53\t`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n54\t\n55\t`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n56\t\n57\t`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n58\t\n59\tPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\n60\trequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\n61\tpull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n62\t`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\n63\tEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n64\t`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\n65\tLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\n66\trewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\n67\t"}]},"parent_t