{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A7NjJBZHWiYSWtGxvxXa7E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Decision\n3\ttype: schema\n4\tentity: Decision\n5\tversion: 1\n6\tschema:\n7\t  decision: string, the choice that was made\n8\t  rationale?: string, why this choice over the alternatives\n9\t  alternative?(array): string, options that were considered and not taken\n10\t  consequence?(array): string, what this decision commits us to\n11\t  context?: string, the situation that prompted the decision\n12\t  affects?(array): Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\n13\t  supersedes?: Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\n14\tsettings:\n15\t  validation: warn\n16\t  frontmatter:\n17\t    status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision): [open, accepted, superseded, rejected]\n18\t    decided?: string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\n19\t    project?: string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t# Decision\n23\t\n24\tA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\n25\tand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\n26\tencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n27\t\n28\tDecisions are found by structured recall:\n29\t`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n30\t\n31\t## What makes a good DecisionNote\n32\t\n33\t- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n34\t- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n35\t  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n36\t- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n37\t- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n38\t\n39\t## Frontmatter\n40\t\n41\t`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\n42\tsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\n